        "description": "Calculate $z + \\bar{z}$."
      },
      "prompt": {
        "question": "What is $z + \\bar{z}$?",
        "hint": "$(3+4i) + (3-4i) = 6$ (imaginary parts cancel)"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$z + \\bar{z} = 6$ (real number, twice the real part)"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$z + \\bar{z} = 8i$ (imaginary)"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$z + \\bar{z} = 6 + 8i$"
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIndex": 0,
      "feedback": {
        "correct": {
          "explanation": "Perfect! $(3+4i) + (3-4i) = 3+3 + (4i-4i) = 6 + 0i = 6$. Imaginary parts cancel!",
          "insight": "General property: $z + \\bar{z} = 2\\text{Re}(z)$ (twice the real part). Always gives a real number."
        },
        "incorrect": {
          "1": "The imaginary parts $4i$ and $-4i$ cancel, they don't add to $8i$!",
          "2": "Add components: $(3+4i) + (3-4i) = 6 + 0i = 6$, not $6+8i$."
        }
      },
      "resultState": {
        "description": "Found z + z̄ = 6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3",
      "order": 3,
      "currentState": {
        "description": "Calculate $z \\cdot \\bar{z}$ and $|z|$."
      },
      "prompt": {
        "question": "What are $z \\cdot \\bar{z}$ and $|z|$?",
        "hint": "$z \\cdot \\bar{z} = (3+4i)(3-4i) = 9 - 16i^2 = 9 + 16 = 25$. So $|z| = \\sqrt{25} = 5$"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$z \\cdot \\bar{z} = 25$ and $|z| = 5$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$z \\cdot \\bar{z} = 7$ and $|z| = \\sqrt{7}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$z \\cdot \\bar{z} = 9 - 16 = -7$"
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIndex": 0,
      "feedback": {
        "correct": {
          "explanation": "Excellent! $(3+4i)(3-4i) = 9 - 12i + 12i - 16i^2 = 9 - 16(-1) = 9 + 16 = 25$. Magnitude: $|z| = \\sqrt{z \\cdot \\bar{z}} = \\sqrt{25} = 5$.",
          "insight": "Key property: $z \\cdot \\bar{z} = |z|^2 = a^2 + b^2$ for $z = a+bi$. This is always a non-negative real number! Also: 3-4-5 is a Pythagorean triple."
        },
        "incorrect": {
          "1": "Expand correctly: $(3+4i)(3-4i) = 9 + 16 = 25$ (difference of squares with $i^2=-1$).",
          "2": "Remember $i^2 = -1$, so $-16i^2 = -16(-1) = +16$. Don't forget this!"
        }
      },
      "resultState": {
        "description": "Found z·z̄ = 25, |z| = 5"
      }
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "keyInsights": [
      "Complex conjugate: $\\overline{a+bi} = a-bi$ (flip sign of imaginary part)",
      "For $z = 3+4i$: $\\bar{z} = 3-4i$",
      "$z + \\bar{z} = 6$ (real, equals $2\\text{Re}(z)$)",
      "$z \\cdot \\bar{z} = 25$ (real, equals $|z|^2$)",
      "Magnitude: $|z| = \\sqrt{z \\cdot \\bar{z}} = \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = 5$",
      "Conjugate is reflection across real axis"
    ],
    "fullSolution": "For z = 3+4i: conjugate z̄ = 3-4i. Sum: z + z̄ = (3+4i) + (3-4i) = 6. Product: z·z̄ = (3+4i)(3-4i) = 9+16 = 25. Magnitude: |z| = √25 = 5.",
